course: dictionary
lesson: 15693
title: Tiresome: boring and annoying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tiresome looks like tired, but it does not mean tired. Use the clues around it. «Sorting one thousand buttons was a tiresome job.» A job with a thousand buttons is slow and dull, so tiresome must mean boring and annoying.
explain: Tiresome can also mean something that makes you feel tired or impatient. «The journey was tiresome, with traffic jams every mile.» The jams make the trip long and irritating, so it is tiresome.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «boring» or «annoying» in place of tiresome. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Tiresome is a little formal, so in your own writing you might choose boring or annoying instead.
fact: Tiresome means boring and annoying, because it goes on too long or happens too often.
fact: Tiresome can also mean making you feel tired or impatient.
fact: Do not confuse tiresome with tired: tired describes how you feel, while tiresome describes the thing that causes the feeling.
fact: «A tiresome job» is a dull job that drags on and on.
fact: Tiresome is a little old-fashioned; children would usually say boring or annoying.
exercise: «Sorting one thousand buttons was a tiresome job.» What does tiresome mean here? | *Boring and annoying, because it goes on too long | Exciting and fun to do | Very quick and easy | Warm and cosy
exercise: «The noisy fly kept buzzing past my ear, which was tiresome.» What does tiresome suggest? | Gentle and quiet | *Irritating, because it keeps happening | Hungry | Something to be proud of
exercise: Which word means the same as tiresome? | Brave | *Boring | Shiny | Cheerful
test: «He kept asking the same question again and again, and it became tiresome.» Why is the question tiresome? | Because it is a secret | *Because it keeps happening and gets annoying | Because it is written in a book | Because it is very kind
test: «The long, slow drive made everyone feel tired and impatient.» What does tiresome mean in «a tiresome drive»? | Quick and short | Colourful | *Long, dull and making you impatient | Full of fun
exam: «The tiresome chore of tidying up went on for hours.» What does tiresome mean? | Sweet-smelling | *Boring and annoying | Hot and sticky | Brilliant
